scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: mash
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 18
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 48.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA security tests explicitly cover ''Silent error swallowing: Config
    IO errors not silently defaulted'' in config_loading.rs and security.rs'
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented 'sanitized Display (CWE-209)' in error.rs. Reviewer verified\
    \ 'CWE-209 error message sanitization \u2014 error.rs:46-78, ServerError inner\
    \ string not exposed'. However, reviewer also noted LOW: NotFound variant is a\
    \ passthrough, so mitigation is incomplete."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Pipeline addressed CWE-113 header injection via runtime sanitization\
    \ (sanitize_header_value), but tenant_id remains a raw String. The finding's core\
    \ issue \u2014 that axiathon-core's validated TenantId is unused, bypassing type-safe\
    \ tenant isolation \u2014 was never flagged. Sanitization mitigates injection\
    \ but doesn't fix the type design violation of SOUL.md Principle #2."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer marked ''VERIFIED: Workspace dependencies properly declared''
    but the ground truth shows 6 deps (clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest,
    toml) use direct versions instead of workspace = true. Reviewer missed this.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''ClientConfig silently ignores unknown
    TOML keys... typos like server_rrl are silently ignored, leading to hard-to-debug
    configuration issues.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote the flawed test containing assert!(config.server().is_none()\
    \ || ...) \u2014 a vacuously true assertion. No phase identified the test as vacuous.\
    \ SOUL.md Principle #4 ('A vacuously true test is worse than no test') was violated\
    \ by the pipeline itself."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'TEA wrote the flawed test with ''let _ = config;'' and zero assertions.
    No phase flagged the test as having no meaningful assertions, despite SOUL.md
    Principle #4 explicitly warning against this pattern.'
